## Attribution

**opencode-rc is inspired by Claude Code's "Channels" feature.** The design of
a chat bridge that dials out to a messaging platform, relays an agent's output,
and turns permission requests into tappable buttons was studied from publicly
available description of how Claude Code's remote-control system behaves.

**No Anthropic code was copied.** Every line in this repository was written from
scratch for this project. Two protocol constants are shared with the Claude
implementation, and we state them plainly so there is no ambiguity later:

| Constant | Value | Why it is not creative expression |
|---|---|---|
| Pairing code length and format | 6 lowercase hex characters from 3 CSPRNG bytes | A code format is a functional specification. Any implementation must interoperate with the same human-facing flow. |
| Permission reply grammar | `/^\s*(y\|yes\|n\|no\|always\|a)\s+([a-km-z]{5})\s*$/i` | A documented wire grammar. |

Neither is copyrightable subject matter; both are the minimum specification
needed for two components to talk to each other. No other part of the Claude
Code implementation was consulted for, or reproduced in, this codebase.

